-- title:
--   Residual absolute irreducibility and oddness from a mod-λ congruence
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$ and a weight $2$ cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalized eigenform for which no proper divisor $M' \mid M$ carries a normalized eigenform with the same $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficients for all primes $\ell \nmid M$. Fix a prime $\lambda$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers. Let $O'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from the Hecke algebra of level $M$ and weight $2$ away from $S$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms generated by the operators [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77) at primes $\ell \nmid M$ outside $S$ together with the $U_q$ at primes $q \mid M$ outside $S$) sending each such $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $O'$. Assume $\lambda \in S$ and that every prime dividing $M$ lies in $S$. Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta \neq 0$ which is a semistable model, in the sense that no prime dividing $\Delta$ divides $c_4$, and with every prime dividing $\Delta$ in $S$; assume $\lambda \neq 2$, that the representation of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on the $\lambda$-torsion of $W$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (points over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is irreducible, and the congruence that for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ outside $S$ the residues in the residue field of $O'$ of $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ and of the trace of Frobenius $a_\ell$ of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$ agree. The conclusion is: for every complete discrete valuation domain $O''$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field which is a module-finite $O'$-algebra via an injective local homomorphism, and every $\lambda$-adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $O''$ (a free $O''$-module of rank $2$ with an adically continuous action of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$), if for every prime $\ell \neq \lambda$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) X + \ell$ (the coefficient taken via $O' \to O''$), then the residual representation of $\rho$, the base change of $\rho$ to the residue field of $O''$, is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure of that residue field, and odd, i.e. $\det \bar\rho(c) = -1$ for every involution $c \neq 1$ in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$.
--
--   This transfers absolute irreducibility and oddness from the mod $\lambda$ representation attached to the semistable model $W$ to the reduction of any $\lambda$-adic representation whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials away from $M\lambda S$ are those prescribed by the newform $g$, which is the form of the hypothesis needed to feed such a representation into the level-lowering machinery. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_level_div_of_isNewform_of_factorization_eq_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_level_div_of_isNewform_of_factorization_eq_two) and by [`WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq).
